    "created_at": "2016-03-22T18:12:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-22T18:12:50Z",
    "body": "This looks good to me. I agree that copy vs. share is confusing. My preferred model would probably be that origin tuples are immutable and that document.domain reassigns the relevant documents' origins to a newly-created tuple. Then you can share with no fear. But based on #794 it sounds like that is not how implementations work. So your strategy of doing copies everywhere except where it's supposed to be explicitly shared seems like the best we can get.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
